==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|fool|proof}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfuːl ˌpɹuːf/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-foolproof.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|of a device}} [[protected|Protected]] against, or [[designed]] to be [[proof]] against, [[misuse]] or [[error]].
# {{lb|en|of an idea or plan}} Certain to succeed in all eventualities, or claimed to be so; [[infallible]].

